Abstractly speaking, an RNN is a function fθ of type (xt,ht)↦(yt,ht+1), where

xt: input vector;
ht: hidden vector;
yt: output vector;
θ: neural network parameters. In words, it is a neural network that maps an input xt into an output yt, with the hidden vector ht playing the role of "memory", a partial record of all previous input-output pairs.

